:NOTE
Amended by No I of the O of 7 June 2024, in force since 1 Nov. 2024 (AS 2024 324).
|

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 10 Duties of the Federal Office of Public Health and of the Coordination Office
1 The Federal Office of Public Health (FOPH) has, in particular, the following duties:
a. it operates a Coordination Office to ensure coordination between ethics committees and other supervisory authorities, as specified in Article 55 paragraph 1 HRA;
b. it oversees the coordination responsibilities delegated to third parties under Article 10a;
c. it issues guidelines concerning the content of the reports to be submitted by the ethics committees in accordance with Article 55 paragraph 2 HRA;
d. it provides information for the public, preparing in particular a summary of the annual reports submitted by ethics committees and a statistical overview of the research projects approved.
2 The Coordination Office, in particular, ensures regular exchanges between the supervisory authorities concerned.
|

:INFO
Art. 10 (continued)
3 It may, in cooperation with the ethics committees and, where appropriate, other supervisory authorities concerned, issue recommendations on approval and notification procedures and on specific aspects of decision-making practice.
|

:INFO
Art. 10a Delegation of coordination responsibilities to the Swiss Association of Research Ethics Committees
1 Coordination between the ethics committees shall be delegated to the Swiss Association of Research Ethics Committees (Swissethics). For its demonstrable efforts in this connection, Swissethics shall receive federal compensation.
2 The details of the delegation of responsibilities and the compensation shall be determined in a public law contract between the FOPH and Swissethics.

